# TDS 9 (determinism, no host-dependent behavior): the grammar artifacts
# embedded into SBOBForge.Parsing must check out byte-identical on every
# platform. git's autocrlf rewrites line endings on Windows checkouts, which
# changes the embedded resource, breaks the frozen grammar-lock sha256 pins,
# and — because emitted profiles embed the whole-lock hash
# (develapp.io/grammar-lock-sha256) — breaks cross-platform drift gates.
# Found dogfooding the Minotaur choco lane (windows runner, Minotaur PR #152):
# the lock pinned the LF checkout hash while the CRLF working-tree file
# hashed differently (exit 5). Treat grammar artifacts as binary: no
# conversion, ever.
*.grammar -text
